 "notes.json": {
  "round1": [
   "These are the bigger copies from your Word files of The Mathematics Curriculum images 6, 14, 15, 19, 21, 23, 115, 121, 128, 135 and 141, and Types of Play image 33 - numbered 1 to 12 on this sheet, in that order. Each is cut to the same part of the picture the page shows now.",
   "I compared every face with the blurred copies on the live pages: this sheet blurs the faces blurred there, apart from the two boys in image 8 who show no face, and leaves clear the ones left clear there.",
   "Left clear, as on the live pages: children seen from behind or looking down with no face showing (for example 2, 9 and 10), the faces printed on a bag in image 2, and the teacher in the mask in image 8.",
   "Image 12 is outdoors: its 7 faces are blurred on the live page too.",
   "Orange faces were added by hand because the face finder missed them. The white outline shows exactly the area blurred.",
   "Remade 25 Oct after your words \"it needs to be precise\": the blur now covers only the eyes with their lids, the nose and the lips - found with a more precise face-point finder - and not the forehead, ears, chin or neck. Where that finder cannot see the face (side views, heads bent down), a small outline over the eyes, nose and mouth is used instead.",
   "After two checks: 8f (the boy in the patterned sweater facing away) and the crouching boy in image 8 show no eyes, nose or mouth, so they are no longer blurred; the face finder's points were wrong on 9a, 12e and 12g, so all their eye, nose and mouth points were placed by hand. (The hand-added face in image 8 is now lettered g.)",
   "Remade on the afternoon of 25 Oct with fixes found by checks on other pages: a face's blurred area now always takes in its own eye, nose and mouth points, and very small faces keep to eyes, nose and mouth with a stronger blur (your \"tiny faces: B\"); no face on this sheet is that small. Where the points were placed by hand (3b, 4a, 7a, 8g, 9a, 12e and 12g), the blurred area now follows those points; 7a's points were placed by hand after a check, so the blur now covers her lower lip. Faces with points from the face finder grew by at most about a fifth (2a, 8a). Please answer this sheet, not the one sent at about 12:05.",
   "Left clear because no face shows enough to recognise: in image 6, the two small girls in the background, top right (side views, looking down at a mat); in image 12, the boy in the green top, bottom right (side or back view). Say if you want either blurred."
  ]
 },
